# The canonical build uses `docker/` as its context (see build-image.yml), so the
# build cannot see application code at all -- there is nothing in docker/ except
# the Dockerfile and requirements.txt. That is structural, not a rule to follow.
#
# This file is the fallback for anyone who builds from the repository root by
# hand. It denies everything and then re-admits only requirements.txt, so a
# root-context build still cannot bake code into the image.
#
# The old .dockerignore carried a warning that `data/` must not be excluded
# wholesale because it was an importable python package sharing a name with the
# artifact directory. That collision is gone by construction: the package is
# src/cleft/data/ and artifacts are data/. Do not reintroduce a flat layout.

*
!docker/requirements.txt
